Two changes that only make sense together, both measured on the eight
2026-07-17 bakeoff maps.

THE DEFAULT FLIPS BACK TO CONNECTIVITY-AWARE, reversing the 2026-06-10 D12
reading ("centrality-ranked everywhere") for compact ONLY, on evidence.
compact's output is consumed as a GRAPH -- it emits induced-subgraph edges,
and its one in-tree diagnostic, hypergumbo_diag.analyze_compact, scores it on
connected components -- but a centrality-ranked prefix of a graph is
frequently not connected. Measured: centrality crops carried 41.9% ISOLATED
nodes at a 25-symbol budget and got WORSE as the budget grew (12.6 -> 23.6 ->
42.1 components at K=25/100/400), where the connected core stays flat
(3.5 -> 4.0 -> 3.2) with isolated at 8.5% -> 2.5% -> 0.3%. sketch keeps
centrality-ranked: it is a reading surface, not a graph. The two surfaces
therefore disagree on their top symbols BY DESIGN, which dissolves WI-zulij's
original complaint rather than resolving it. --connectivity stays accepted as
an explicit no-op (it shipped in v7.0.0); --no-connectivity opts into
centrality-ranked selection matching the sketch.

CONNECTIVITY GAINED THE CONTAINMENT PROPERTY WI-vofud THOUGHT IT COULD NOT
HAVE: nodes(K1) subset-of nodes(K2) went 55/120 budget pairs -> 120/120,
pretix included. WI-vofud's recorded justification -- "bridge expansion is not
a ranked prefix, so budget-containment was never that mode's contract" -- is
FALSE, and had been quoted as settled for two sessions. The greedy loop never
reads the budget (max_additional appears only in its while guard), so bridge
expansion was ALREADY prefix-nested: with any budget-independent seed set,
containment measures 120/120 on unchanged code. What broke it was the en-bloc,
budget-SIZED seed preload -- admitting every seed before the first pick handed
the scorer a different union-find state at every budget, producing a different
SEQUENCE of picks rather than a longer one. Porting WI-vofud's monotone seed
QUOTA moves 65 violations to 66; the seed ORDER was never the problem.

THE FIX IS AN INTERLEAVE, NOT A CAP. Seeds are metered into one
budget-independent stream -- fixed seed order (entrypoints by confidence, then
cross-cutting endpoints by edge count) alternating 1:2 with greedy bridge
picks -- so the budget becomes pure truncation and a smaller budget's node list
is an ordered PREFIX of a larger one's. The old adaptive entrypoint cap (1/3 vs
1/2, switching regimes on len(eps) > max_symbols) is deleted: alternation
guarantees bridges a slot rather than leaving them the remainder, which serves
the keycloak case the cap was written for more directly. The 1:2 ratio is
TUNED -- at 1:1 a seed can be admitted and then have both neighbours out-scored
globally, stranding it (14 singletons per 100 nodes on the keycloak fixture);
1:2 drops that to 1, and 1:3/1:4 buy nothing. Any FIXED ratio preserves
containment, so the ratio is a pure quality knob. WI-nivuj determinism is
untouched: scorer, sorted-frontier iteration and strict > tie-break reused
verbatim. Seed and pick admission now share one _admit step, so they cannot
drift.

COST, stated plainly. Fragmentation is unchanged-to-better vs the old
connectivity policy, and entrypoint reachability IMPROVES at small budgets
(62.0% -> 80.0% at K=25). The one real cost is a boundary artifact: truncating
a stream can land on a seed, so the FINAL emitted node may have no edge --
measured as exactly one singleton at index 99 of 100. It cannot be
special-cased away, because "don't take a seed in the last slot" is a
budget-DEPENDENT decision and reintroducing budget-dependence is what broke
containment. The keycloak test's `singletons == 0` is relaxed to "at most the
final emitted node", with the reasoning recorded in place and a positional
assertion so a singleton anywhere else still fails.

The preceding filter unification (#155) narrowed compact's default population,
which raised centrality-mode fragmentation by dropping file-kind hub nodes.
With this flip that narrowing lands on --no-connectivity, whose stated job is
now precisely "matching the sketch", so dropping the nodes sketch drops is
correct for that mode. Every default consumer is strictly better off
(isolated 17.6% -> 0.3% at K=400).

